## 2. Comparable contract (new scenarios)

"Sync" is the completion witness. No scenario uses a sleep to establish an order, and no order between concurrent senders is
imposed or asserted. Upstream references are paths under `upstream/pekko`.

| Scenario | Guarantee, Pekko reference | Preconditions and sync | Allowed | Forbidden | Intentional Go difference |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| S19 external stop | G5: `docs/src/main/paradox/actors.md:923-957` (stop via `ActorRefFactory`, current message continues, queued messages are not processed, dead-lettered); `actor/.../actor/ActorSystem.scala:939-948` and `actor/.../actor/dungeon/Dispatch.scala:167-169` (external `stop` sends `Terminate`) | Concurrent: `M1` is held inside `Receive` until the stop is accepted; `M2` and `M3` are queued behind it first. Controlled: `M1` runs and returns (one thread cannot hold it). The stop is called from the test goroutine, not from the actor. Sync: `Done` / `Terminated` probe, then `M5` is sent to the stopped actor | `M1` finishes before `post-stop-begin`; `M2`, `M3` dead-lettered at most once; `M5` dead-lettered (exactly once in controlled mode) | `M2` or `M3` received; `post-stop` missing or repeated; a message both received and dead-lettered | none |
| S20 stop before the first activation (D2) | G5.e: `actor/.../actor/dungeon/Dispatch.scala:79-111` (`Create` is enqueued ahead of any `Terminate`), `actor/.../actor/dungeon/FaultHandling.scala:247-254` (`postStop`) | Concurrent only. Pekko: the actor lives on a one-thread dispatcher whose thread a blocker actor holds, so `Create` cannot run; `M1` is queued, the stop is sent, then the blocker is released. Go: the system runs on a held executor, so `Spawn`'s first activation cannot run until released. Both sides check that no event of the actor exists before the release; otherwise the run is a harness error | `pre-start`, `post-stop-begin`, `post-stop` once each, in that order; `M1` dead-lettered once, never received | `pre-start` or `post-stop` missing, repeated, or out of order | **D2**, see section 5 |
| S21 serial processing | G3.c: `docs/src/main/paradox/general/actors.md:56-62`; `actor/.../dispatch/Mailbox.scala:187-195` (`setAsScheduled`), `:230-240` (`run`) | Concurrent only. Three senders each send four messages and a sentinel to one receiver whose handler yields the processor 50 times between `received` and `received-end`. Sync: three sentinels received | any interleaving between senders | a `received` of the receiver while an earlier `received` of it has no `received-end` yet | none |

S21 is a negative property: the absence of an overlap in the runs is evidence, not a proof, and it depends on the handler
giving a second worker time to enter.

